        <obo:remark>EDAM Bioimaging is an extension to the EDAM ontology (edamontology.org) dedicated to imaging and (bio)image informatics. It has been developed by an open, global community of contributors, including consortia and projects such as NEUBIAS/GloBIAS, COMULIS, ELIXIR, Euro-BioImaging, vEM, QUAREP-LiMi, foundingGIDE, EOSC OSCARS, and more.</obo:remark>
        <obo:remark>October 2025: EDAM Bioimaging is in the stage of final refinements towards the first full production version. The production version will include persistent, resolvable identifiers for all concepts; a merged version with the main EDAM; and coverage of microscopy across bio- and other sciences (e.g. materials science and solid-state physics, chemistry, geology, archaeology, cultural heritage), and both clinical and preclinical medical imaging. Further additions and refinements are planned after the production release.</obo:remark>
